issue.body:
### Describe the bug

Consider a class:

```java
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;
import javax.enterprise.inject.Vetoed;
import org.slf4j.Logger;
import org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;

@Vetoed
class A {
    private static final Logger LOG = LoggerFactory.getLogger(A.class);
    public static AtomicInteger count = new AtomicInteger(0);

    A() {
        LOG.info("{} constructed", this.getClass().getSimpleName());
        count.incrementAndGet();
    }

    public int getCount() {
        return A.count.get();
    }
}
```

Some bean with a scoped producer:
```java
import javax.enterprise.context.ApplicationScoped;
import javax.enterprise.inject.Produces;

@ApplicationScoped
class Producer {
    @Produces
    @ApplicationScoped
    A produce() {
        return new A();
    }
}
```

And a unit test:
```java
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertEquals;
import javax.inject.Inject;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import io.quarkus.test.junit.QuarkusTest;

@QuarkusTest
class ATest {
    @Inject
    A a;

    @Test
    void test() {
        assertEquals(1, a.getCount());
    }
}
```

The constructor will be invoked twice - once on creation of the client proxy for the application scope and once when creating the actual object.

### Expected behavior

Non-bean noargs constructor is not called or only pseudo scopes (`@Dependent`) are allowed for producers returning non-bean objects.

### Actual behavior

The test fails with:
> org.opentest4j.AssertionFailedError: expected: <1> but was: <2>

And it logs:

> 2021-11-19 11:59:46,732 INFO  [org.acm.cdi.pro.A] (main) Producer_ProducerMethod_produce_e48d74bd24e672937bf49c60afc6db55ea4584ea_ClientProxy constructed
> 2021-11-19 11:59:46,755 INFO  [org.acm.cdi.pro.A] (main) A constructed

Because the non-bean noargs constructor is called when the client proxy is constructed.

### How to Reproduce?

Run the unit test from the description above.

### Output of `uname -a` or `ver`

